    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0530" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-12T22:00:00-04:00">May 12, 1941—10 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>292. Your 406 and 411, both of May 5, and the Department’s 277 of May 7.<anchor
                        n="60" xml:id="d529-f1"/> It is hoped that at least as a preliminary
                    precaution it will be possible to keep the Air France stocks of aviation
                    gasoline out of the hands of Lufthansa<anchor n="61" xml:id="d529-f2"/> and
                    similar organizations.</p>
                <p>This Government feels that it would be most prejudicial to the defense of the
                    United States for Lufthansa to resume trans-Atlantic operations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d529-f1" n="60" xml:id="d529-f1-content">
                <p>None printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d529-f2" n="61" xml:id="d529-f2-content">
                <p>The Deutsche Lufthansa was the outstanding company in pre-war German commercial
                    aviation.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
